<title>SINGAPORE: SINGAPORE MANUFACTURING OUTPUT UP 9.3 PCT IN JUNE.</title>
<headline>SINGAPORE MANUFACTURING OUTPUT UP 9.3 PCT IN JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's manufacturing output grew 9.3 percent in June year-on-year, the Economic Development Board (EDB) said in a statement on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The EDB said the increase in June partially alleviated a decline in previous months, leading to a cumulative decline of 1.1 percent year-on-year for the first six months of 1997.</p>
<p>Manufacturing output fell 1.2 percent in May.</p>
<p>The EDB said export orders boosted output of electronics products and components by 11.8 percent year-on-year in June.</p>
<p>Table of selected Singapore industries:</p>
<p>				    (pct change over previous year)</p>
<p>				    Jun 97	 May 97	  Apr 97</p>
<p>   *Total manufacturing	 9.3	   -1.2	    1.6</p>
<p>    Electronics		  11.8	     0	     3.9</p>
<p>    Petroleum products	 -5.4	    0.3	  -13.6</p>
<p>    Pharmaceuticals	    48.0	  -12.2	   13.3</p>
<p>    Industrial chemicals     14.5	    8.2	   15.2</p>
<p>    Petrochemicals	     70.9	   33.7	   11.1</p>
<p>    Machinery x-electronics   7.2	   -4.2	   -1.1</p>
<p>    Transport equipment	15.2	    0.8	    5.4</p>
<p>    Fabricated metals	  -3.2	  -13.9	  -11.7</p>
<p>    Printing/publishing	 3.1	    7.5	    5.6</p>
<p>    Food &amp; Beverages	   -8.2	   -3.9	   -0.9</p>
<p>    Electrical machines	 1.3	    3.5	   -1.9</p>
<p>    Plastic products	   -6.8	   -7.0	   -7.6</p>
<p>* Total manufacturing output excludes rubber processing.</p>
